      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name}: Hey Fax!\n\nAs far as I'm aware, this report is mostly related to how you cannot use Final IK scripts on humanoid bones or children of humanoid bones. (This also prevents you from targeting or referencing them too). The date this was posted is also close to when Networked IK came out, which was the cause of this bug. My best guess for why this occurs is because while all the humanoid bones are networked, the Final IK scripts are not, and the lack of communication between the two results in undesirable behavior.\n\nSo while the report is very old, the same problem exists and has not been remedied by IK 2.0, so marking as complete feels wrong.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
